gtk3dialog (1.0.0-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Wayland anchoring. <window> now accepts three attributes, layer=, edge=
    and dist=, which turn the dialog into a wlr-layer-shell surface: a bar, a
    dock, a desktop widget. Ported from the BunsenLabs gtk3dialog fork
    (GPL-2+) with two corrections to the original code:
    - the dist= margin was parsed into an unsigned type and then checked with
      "< 0", a test that can never fire, so an out-of-range value wrapped
      around silently instead of falling back to the default; it is now
      parsed with strtol(), rejects trailing garbage and is clamped to
      [0, 200];
    - the Wayland check read the GDK_BACKEND environment variable and
      proceeded whenever it was unset, which is the normal case under X11;
      the library is now asked directly (gtk_layer_is_supported()), so an
      X11 session or a Wayland compositor without the protocol falls back to
      an ordinary window with a single diagnostic instead of a burst of
      CRITICAL warnings from gtk-layer-shell.
  * Build. New optional dependency gtk-layer-shell >= 0.8.0, wired into
    autotools and CMake; ./configure --without-layer-shell builds without it,
    and the three attributes are then ignored at runtime.
  * Documentation. haplo-dialog-xml(5) documents layer=, edge= and dist=;
    examples/layer-shell shows a bar, a dock and a wallpaper strip.
  * Unlike 1.0.0-2 and 1.0.0-3, this revision does change the binary.
  * Verified. The anchoring is exercised under sway 1.12 (wlroots 0.20) on a
    headless 1280x720 output and measured to the pixel: a topstride bar flush
    across the full width, a bottom dock exactly dist= pixels off the edge, a
    background strip entirely covered by an ordinary window, and dist=0 against
    dist=60 separated by exactly 60 px. Not covered: multi-output, real
    hardware, and compositors outside wlroots such as Hyprland.

 -- haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>  Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:43:05 +0200

gtk3dialog (1.0.0-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Public identity. The Maintainer field and the changelog signatures now use
    the project identity, haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>, instead of a
    personal name and a company domain that shipped to every installation and
    showed up in "apt show gtk3dialog".
  * Packaging metadata. Vcs-Git and Vcs-Browser point at the real repository,
    https://gitlab.com/haplo-dialog/gtk3dialog; they previously referenced a
    forge that never existed.
  * No functional change: the built binary is identical to 1.0.0-2.

 -- haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 20:52:43 +0200

gtk3dialog (1.0.0-2) unstable; urgency=high

  * Security hardening pass (pre-publication audit, 2026-08-11):
    - automaton.c: bound _sum() to MAXWIDGETS to prevent a stack buffer
      overflow when a container holds more than 256 direct child widgets
      (CWE-787).
    - variables.c: replace an unterminated strncpy() into variable->Name
      with g_strlcpy() (CWE-125/CWE-170).
    - widget_terminal.c: size argv[]/envv[] with a guaranteed NULL terminator
      so the vte spawn never reads past the array (CWE-170).
    - safe_exec.c: wire the previously-dead _build_child_env() into both spawn
      paths so spawned children no longer inherit the multi-KiB DIALOG blob
      (avoids spurious E2BIG); free the built environment on all paths.
    - actions.c: fix the append action's first-operand copy offset (functional
      bug on indented XML).
    - automaton.c: drop two per-instruction memory leaks (a redundant g_malloc
      before strdup, and leaked strdup()s passed to new_tag_attributeset()).
    - widgets.c: correct a misleading comment about shell-injection safety.
    - gtk3dialog.1: document HAPLO_NO_SHELL_FALLBACK in the ENVIRONMENT section.
  * Packaging: move the source-stanza build dependencies from the invalid
    "Depends" field to "Build-Depends" (silences dpkg-gencontrol's
    "unknown information field Depends" warning); drop the now-redundant
    debian/compat file (compat level set via debhelper-compat in Build-Depends).

 -- haplo-dialog <devel@haplo-dialog.fr>  Tue, 11 Aug 2026 11:05:32 +0200

gtk3dialog (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging for gtk3dialog — haplo-dialog fork.
  * GTK3 dialog window creator for shell scripts.
  * Toolkit: GTK3.
  * Security hardening: safe_exec, FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, PIE, Full RELRO,
    stack-protector-strong.

